; host/supervisor.bl — the pinned HOST MODULE for `Elixir.BeamLisp.Supervisor`.
;
; `lib/beam_lisp/supervisor.ex` lowers a supervision tree — a strategy keyword
; plus a list of child specs — into a REAL OTP supervisor. The language reaches
; it two ways: `rt.bl`'s `core` table binds the names `supervise`/`worker` to
; `Elixir.BeamLisp.Supervisor.supervise/2,3` and `.worker/2,3` (VALUE rows,
; external funs over the pinned beam), and `priv/std/proc/super.bl` +
; `priv/lib/live/app.bl` call `server/2,3,4`, `pool/5` and `start_link/1`
; directly. This file is the `.bl` port of that module, compiled by
; `BeamLisp.AOT/compile_host_file` into ONE exact-named beam whose export
; surface is the live module's, datum for datum.
;
; (This wave owns source and tests only; the seed entry that points the real
; atom at this file is written by the wave that deletes `supervisor.ex`. That
; entry needs NO compile option — the module is FUNCTIONS-ONLY: no struct to
; synthesize, no behaviour to record, no macro to export.)
;
; WHAT THE MODULE OWES, clause for clause:
;
;   * `worker/2,3` — the child spec `%{id: id, start: start_spec(start)}` plus
;     the three optional keys (`:restart`, `:shutdown`, `:type`). `start` is
;     either a ZERO-ARITY function, wrapped as `{Task, :start_link, [start]}`
;     (the plainest BEAM worker), or an explicit `{m, f, args}` MFA tuple passed
;     through untouched, so any OTP process with a `start_link/1` is
;     superviseable. Anything else is the live `start_spec/1`
;     `FunctionClauseError`.
;
;   * `maybe_put/3` is `Map.get(opts, key)`: a MISSING key and a key whose value
;     is `nil` are the same fact — the option is absent — which is why the check
;     is `Map.get` and never `:maps.get` (the latter raises `badkey`).
;
;   * `supervise/2,3` — `Supervisor.start_link/2` of the child list, strategy
;     normalized, restart-intensity options appended, and the `{:ok, pid}`
;     UNWRAPPED so the tree hands the caller its handle directly. A start that
;     does NOT answer `{:ok, pid}` is the live `MatchError` — built here as the
;     struct the BEAM would have built, `term` and `__exception__` included, so
;     `Exception.message/1` renders the same text.
;
;   * `server/2,3,4` + `start_server/3` — a defserver child IS the gen_server,
;     never a wrapper task. A bare-fn child runs the fn as a `Task` and a
;     `:permanent` supervisor restarts it forever the moment the fn returns; so
;     the defserver child is an MFA tuple pointing at `start_server/3`, whose
;     `{:ok, pid}` is the shape OTP requires. `:name` (optional) is passed
;     through to `BeamLisp.Server.start_link/3`, so a singleton child stays
;     addressable by name across its own restarts.
;
;   * `pool/5` — a named one-for-one sub-supervisor owning one dispatcher (init
;     arg = the pool's registered name) and `n` identical workers (each handed
;     its index). The whole sub-tree is ONE child of the parent: it restarts and
;     dies as a unit. The worker ids are `w0`, `w1`, … — `String.to_atom` of
;     `"w#{i}"`, the live spelling; the index range is `0..(n-1)`, whose
;     DESCENDING behaviour for `n < 1` (`0..-1` enumerates `[0, -1]`) is the
;     live behaviour and is reproduced here through the same `Range`.
;
;   * `start_named_sup/2` — `Supervisor.start_link/2` with
;     `strategy: :one_for_one, name: name`, the child-start entry of a pool spec.
;
;   * `start_link/1` — the entry `BeamLisp.Server.start_link/3` dispatches to
;     when its argument carries the `__supervisor__` marker (what
;     `proc.super/defsupervisor` builds). Head: a map with `:strategy` AND
;     `:children`; anything else is the live `FunctionClauseError`. Intensity
;     lives under `:intensity` as a `BeamLisp.Vector` whose `:items` is a
;     2-tuple; ANY other shape falls to the live `_ -> []` catch-all, which is
;     why the check is one boolean and not a clause chain.
;
; GUARDS AND CLAUSE HEADS BECOME BODY CHECKS. A pinned `.bl` parameter pattern
; compiles to a body-level match, not a clause head, so every guard
; (`is_map(opts)`, `is_atom(strategy)`, `is_list(list)`, `is_atom(name)`) and
; every multi-clause dispatch (`start_spec/1`, `child_list/1`,
; `intensity_from/1`, `start_server/3`, the `%{strategy: …, children: …}` head)
; is written as an explicit `if`/`cond` and raises the SAME
; `FunctionClauseError` — module, function and arity — the BEAM raised, named
; with THIS beam's own atom (read from a fun literal compiled into this file,
; the `seq_cursor.bl`/`vector.bl` idiom) so a probe compile names the probe
; atom.
;
; NO TOP-LEVEL HELPERS. A pinned module's export surface IS the file's top-level
; defns (`defn-` is NOT privatized on this path), and the live module's private
; helpers are not exports. Every helper is therefore a LOCAL closure, rebuilt
; inside the public fn that needs it, so `module_info(:exports)` of this beam is
; `module_info(:exports)` of the live module minus the Elixir-generated
; `__info__/1`.
;
; THE MODULE NAME IS ALSO THE OTP APPLICATION'S REGISTERED SUPERVISOR NAME.
; `BeamLisp.Application.start/2` starts the runtime's ONE supervisor with
; `name: BeamLisp.Supervisor`, so `Process.whereis(BeamLisp.Supervisor)` is a
; live pid in any booted VM. Registering a NAME and loading a MODULE share an
; atom and nothing else: no function here touches that process, and nothing here
; ever starts a supervision tree under that name — `supervise/2,3` and
; `start_link/1` start UNREGISTERED supervisors, and the only registered trees
; this module starts are the caller's own `pool/5` names. The test suite pins
; that separation explicitly.
;
; RUNTIME-TIER, NOT BOOT-TIER. Every caller is language/library code that runs
; after `BeamLisp.init/0` has interned the prelude — `rt.bl`'s link table holds
; the atoms, and `proc.super`/`app.bl` call them at runtime. So `(list …)` and
; `(tuple …)` may lower to `BeamLisp.Ns.Core` (on the code path before the
; application starts; the same shape `priv/host/application.bl` ships) and the
; `(defn …)` bodies may call host modules (`Supervisor`, `Task`, `BeamLisp.Server`,
; `BeamLisp.Vector`, `String`, `Atom`, `Map`, `Range`, `Enum`). No `str` var is
; used: the two places the live module interpolates build the same binary from
; `String.Chars`/`iolist_to_binary`, which needs no var table.
;
; Run: bin/bl test test/bl/host_supervisor_test.bl

(ns host.supervisor)

(defn worker
  "Build a child spec for one worker: `%{id: id, start: start_spec(start)}`,
   plus the optional `:restart`/`:shutdown`/`:type` keys the caller passes.

   `start` is a ZERO-ARITY function — wrapped as a `Task` process running it —
   or an explicit `{module, fun, args}` MFA tuple, passed through untouched.
   Anything else is the live `start_spec/1` `FunctionClauseError`; a
   non-map `opts` is the live `worker/3` one."
  ([id start]
   (let [own (erlang/element 2 (erlang/fun_info (fn [] nil) :module))
         fce (fn [fname arity]
               (erlang/error
                 (Elixir.FunctionClauseError/exception
                   (list (tuple :module own)
                         (tuple :function fname)
                         (tuple :arity arity)))))
         start-spec
         (fn [start]
           (cond
             (erlang/is_function start 0)
             (tuple :"Elixir.Task" :start_link (list start))

             (and (erlang/is_tuple start)
                  (erlang/== 3 (erlang/tuple_size start))
                  (erlang/is_atom (erlang/element 1 start))
                  (erlang/is_atom (erlang/element 2 start))
                  (erlang/is_list (erlang/element 3 start)))
             (tuple (erlang/element 1 start)
                    (erlang/element 2 start)
                    (erlang/element 3 start))

             :else (fce :start_spec 1)))]
     (maps/put :start (start-spec start) (maps/put :id id (maps/new)))))
  ([id start opts]
   (let [own (erlang/element 2 (erlang/fun_info (fn [] nil) :module))
         fce (fn [fname arity]
               (erlang/error
                 (Elixir.FunctionClauseError/exception
                   (list (tuple :module own)
                         (tuple :function fname)
                         (tuple :arity arity)))))
         start-spec
         (fn [start]
           (cond
             (erlang/is_function start 0)
             (tuple :"Elixir.Task" :start_link (list start))

             (and (erlang/is_tuple start)
                  (erlang/== 3 (erlang/tuple_size start))
                  (erlang/is_atom (erlang/element 1 start))
                  (erlang/is_atom (erlang/element 2 start))
                  (erlang/is_list (erlang/element 3 start)))
             (tuple (erlang/element 1 start)
                    (erlang/element 2 start)
                    (erlang/element 3 start))

             :else (fce :start_spec 1)))
         maybe-put
         (fn [spec key]
           (let [value (Map/get opts key)]
             (if (erlang/== nil value) spec (maps/put key value spec))))]
     (if (erlang/is_map opts)
       (maybe-put (maybe-put (maybe-put (maps/put :start (start-spec start)
                                                  (maps/put :id id (maps/new)))
                                        :restart)
                             :shutdown)
                  :type)
       (fce :worker 3)))))

(defn supervise
  "Start a supervision tree. Returns the supervisor pid — the `{:ok, pid}` is
   UNWRAPPED, so the tree hands the caller its handle directly.

   `strategy` is the beam-lisp-spelled atom (`:one-for-one`); it is normalized
   to Elixir's underscore spelling before it reaches `Supervisor.start_link/2`.
   `opts` may carry the dashed beam-lisp keys `:max-restarts`/`:max-seconds`,
   which become the supervisor's `:max_restarts`/`:max_seconds` — in THAT order,
   and only when their value is not `nil`. A non-atom strategy is the live
   `supervise/2` (or `supervise/3`) `FunctionClauseError`; a child list that is
   neither a `BeamLisp.Vector` nor an Erlang list is the live
   `child_list/1` one."
  ([strategy children]
   (if (erlang/is_atom strategy)
     (supervise strategy children (maps/new))
     (let [own (erlang/element 2 (erlang/fun_info (fn [] nil) :module))]
       (erlang/error
         (Elixir.FunctionClauseError/exception
           (list (tuple :module own)
                 (tuple :function :supervise)
                 (tuple :arity 2)))))))
  ([strategy children opts]
   (if (erlang/is_atom strategy)
     (let [own (erlang/element 2 (erlang/fun_info (fn [] nil) :module))
           fce (fn [fname arity]
                 (erlang/error
                   (Elixir.FunctionClauseError/exception
                     (list (tuple :module own)
                           (tuple :function fname)
                           (tuple :arity arity)))))
           normalize (fn [strategy]
                       (String/to_atom (String/replace (Atom/to_string strategy) "-" "_")))
           child-list
           (fn [children]
             (if (and (erlang/is_map children)
                      (erlang/is_map_key :__struct__ children)
                      (erlang/== :"Elixir.BeamLisp.Vector" (erlang/map_get :__struct__ children)))
               (BeamLisp.Vector/to_list children)
               (if (erlang/is_list children) children (fce :child_list 1))))
           intensity-opts
           (fn []
             (Enum/reduce
               (list (tuple :"max-restarts" :max_restarts) (tuple :"max-seconds" :max_seconds))
               (list)
               (fn [pair acc]
                 (let [key (erlang/element 1 pair)
                       opt (erlang/element 2 pair)
                       value (Map/get opts key)]
                   (if (erlang/== nil value)
                     acc
                     (erlang/++ acc (list (tuple opt value))))))))
           match-error
           (fn [term]
             (maps/put :term term
               (maps/put :__exception__ true
                 (maps/put :__struct__ :"Elixir.MatchError" (maps/new)))))
           sup-opts (erlang/++ (list (tuple :strategy (normalize strategy))) (intensity-opts))
           result (if (Process/get :bl_generation)
                    (tuple :ok (start_link
                      {:strategy strategy :children (child-list children)
                       :intensity (BeamLisp.Vector/new (list (Map/get opts :max-restarts 3) (Map/get opts :max-seconds 5)))}))
                    (Supervisor/start_link (child-list children) sup-opts))]
       (if (and (erlang/is_tuple result)
                (erlang/== 2 (erlang/tuple_size result))
                (erlang/== :ok (erlang/element 1 result)))
         (erlang/element 2 result)
         (erlang/error (match-error result))))
     (let [own (erlang/element 2 (erlang/fun_info (fn [] nil) :module))]
       (erlang/error
         (Elixir.FunctionClauseError/exception
           (list (tuple :module own)
                 (tuple :function :supervise)
                 (tuple :arity 3))))))))

(defn server
  "Child spec for a defserver child: the child IS the gen_server, not a wrapper.

   A bare-fn child (`worker/2`) runs the fn as a `Task` — right for a loop,
   wrong for a gen_server: the fn would return the pid, the task would exit
   `:normal`, and a `:permanent` supervisor would restart it forever. So a
   defserver child is an MFA tuple pointing here, and `start_server/3` returns
   the `{:ok, pid}` shape OTP requires."
  ([id mod] (server id mod nil (maps/new)))
  ([id mod arg] (server id mod arg (maps/new)))
  ([id mod arg opts]
   (let [own (erlang/element 2 (erlang/fun_info (fn [] nil) :module))
         fce (fn [fname arity]
               (erlang/error
                 (Elixir.FunctionClauseError/exception
                   (list (tuple :module own)
                         (tuple :function fname)
                         (tuple :arity arity)))))
         maybe-put
         (fn [spec key]
           (let [value (Map/get opts key)]
             (if (erlang/== nil value) spec (maps/put key value spec))))]
     (if (erlang/is_map opts)
       (maybe-put (maybe-put (maybe-put (maps/put :start
                                                  (tuple own :start_server
                                                         ;; The supervisor may predate this namespace/realm. Carry the spec
                                                         ;; creator's bindings into initial starts and OTP restarts.
                                                         (list mod arg (tuple :"$bl_supervised_context" (BeamLisp.Env/capture) (Map/get opts :name))))
                                                  (maps/put :id id (maps/new)))
                                        :restart)
                             :shutdown)
                  :type)
       (fce :server 4)))))

(defn- server_name? [name]
  (or (erlang/== nil name) (erlang/is_atom name)
      (and (erlang/is_tuple name) (erlang/== 2 (erlang/tuple_size name))
           (or (erlang/== :global (erlang/element 1 name))
               (and (erlang/== :local (erlang/element 1 name)) (erlang/is_atom (erlang/element 2 name)))))
      (and (erlang/is_tuple name) (erlang/== 3 (erlang/tuple_size name))
           (erlang/== :via (erlang/element 1 name)) (erlang/is_atom (erlang/element 2 name)))))

(defn start_server
  "The child-start entry of a defserver child spec (see `server/4`). `name` is an
   optional OTP name — a singleton child (a registry, a named bus) stays
   addressable across restarts. Supports the same nil/atom and native local,
   global and via name terms as Server.start_link; malformed values retain the
   start_server/3 FunctionClauseError."
  [mod arg name]
  (cond
    (and (erlang/is_tuple name) (erlang/== 3 (erlang/tuple_size name))
         (erlang/== :"$bl_supervised_context" (erlang/element 1 name)))
    (let [previous (BeamLisp.Env/capture)]
      (try
        (BeamLisp.Env/bind (erlang/element 2 name))
        (if (Process/get :bl_generation)
          (BeamLisp.Env/with_supervisor_execution!
            (fn [] (start_server mod arg (erlang/element 3 name))))
          (start_server mod arg (erlang/element 3 name)))
        (finally (BeamLisp.Env/bind previous))))
    (erlang/== nil name)
    (tuple :ok (BeamLisp.Server/start_link mod arg))

    (server_name? name)
    (tuple :ok (BeamLisp.Server/start_link mod arg (maps/put :name name (maps/new))))

    :else
    (let [own (erlang/element 2 (erlang/fun_info (fn [] nil) :module))]
      (erlang/error
        (Elixir.FunctionClauseError/exception
          (list (tuple :module own)
                (tuple :function :start_server)
                (tuple :arity 3)))))))

(defn pool
  "Child spec for a POOL: a named one-for-one sub-supervisor owning one
   dispatcher (whose init arg is the pool's registered name) and `n` identical
   workers (each receives its index as init arg). The whole sub-tree is one
   child: it restarts and dies as a unit."
  [id sup_name dispatcher_mod target n]
  (let [own (erlang/element 2 (erlang/fun_info (fn [] nil) :module))
        worker-spec
        (fn [i]
          (server (String/to_atom (erlang/iolist_to_binary
                                    (list "w" (String.Chars/to_string i))))
                  target
                  i))
        dispatcher (maps/put :start
                             (tuple own :start_server (list dispatcher_mod sup_name nil))
                             (maps/put :id :dispatcher (maps/new)))
        children (erlang/++
                   (list dispatcher)
                   (Enum/map (Enum/to_list (Range/new 0 (erlang/- n 1))) worker-spec))]
    (maps/put :start
              (tuple own :start_named_sup (list children sup_name))
              (maps/put :type :supervisor (maps/put :id id (maps/new))))))

(defn start_named_sup
  "The child-start entry of a pool spec: start the named one-for-one
   sub-supervisor."
  [children name]
  (if (Process/get :bl_generation)
    (BeamLisp.Env/with_supervisor_execution!
      (fn [] (start_managed_tree children
               (list (tuple :strategy :one_for_one) (tuple :name name)) (BeamLisp.Env/capture))))
    (Supervisor/start_link children (list (tuple :strategy :one_for_one) (tuple :name name)))))

(defn- managed_children [children context generation depth remaining]
  ;; Validate the ENTIRE tree before OTP starts its first child. Only these
  ;; two fixed native entrypoints are accepted; no caller-nominated callback.
  (when (or (erlang/> depth 64) (erlang/< remaining 0)) (erlang/error :supervisor_child_budget))
  (let [items (cond
                (and (erlang/is_map children)
                     (erlang/== :Elixir.BeamLisp.Vector (Map/get children :__struct__)))
                  (BeamLisp.Vector/to_list children)
                (erlang/is_list children) children
                :else (erlang/error :unmanaged_supervisor_child))]
    (Enum/map_reduce items remaining
      (fn [child left]
        (when (or (erlang/=< left 0) (not (erlang/is_map child)))
          (erlang/error :unmanaged_supervisor_child))
        (let [mfa (Map/get child :start)
              _ (when-not (and (erlang/is_tuple mfa) (erlang/== 3 (erlang/tuple_size mfa))
                               (erlang/== :Elixir.BeamLisp.Supervisor (erlang/element 1 mfa))
                               (erlang/is_list (erlang/element 3 mfa)))
                  (erlang/error :unmanaged_supervisor_child))
              entry (erlang/element 2 mfa) args (erlang/element 3 mfa)]
          (cond
            (and (erlang/== :start_server entry) (erlang/== 3 (erlang/length args)))
              (let [mod (erlang/hd args) name (erlang/hd (erlang/tl (erlang/tl args)))
                    bare (if (and (erlang/is_tuple name) (erlang/== 3 (erlang/tuple_size name))
                                  (erlang/== :"$bl_supervised_context" (erlang/element 1 name)))
                           (erlang/element 3 name) name)]
                (when-not (server_name? bare) (erlang/error :invalid_supervisor_child_name))
                (when (not (Enum/member? (Map/get generation :modules) mod))
                  (BeamLisp.Env/prepare_sdk_class! mod))
                (BeamLisp.Env/assert_managed_server_class! generation mod)
                (tuple (Map/put child :start (tuple :Elixir.BeamLisp.Supervisor :start_server
                          (list mod (erlang/hd (erlang/tl args))
                            (tuple :"$bl_supervised_context" context bare)))) (erlang/- left 1)))
            (and (erlang/== :start_named_sup entry) (erlang/== 2 (erlang/length args)))
              (let [nested (managed_children (erlang/hd args) context generation (erlang/+ depth 1)
                              (erlang/- left 1))
                    name (erlang/hd (erlang/tl args))]
                (when-not (erlang/is_atom name) (erlang/error :invalid_supervisor_name))
                (tuple (Map/put child :start (tuple :Elixir.BeamLisp.Supervisor :start_named_sup
                         (list (erlang/element 1 nested) name))) (erlang/element 2 nested)))
            :else (erlang/error :unmanaged_supervisor_child)))))))

(defn init
  "Native managed supervisor callback. Claim before context/user child starts,
   publish monitored whole-G owner, then hand exact child specs to real OTP."
  [argument]
  (when-not (and (erlang/is_tuple argument) (erlang/== 5 (erlang/tuple_size argument))
                (erlang/== :bl_managed_supervisor (erlang/element 1 argument)))
    (erlang/error :unadmitted_supervisor_starter))
  (let [context (BeamLisp.Env/claim_supervisor_start! (erlang/element 2 argument))]
    (when-not (erlang/== context (erlang/element 3 argument))
      (erlang/error :supervisor_start_context_mismatch))
    (BeamLisp.Env/bind context)
    (let [generation (Process/get :bl_generation)
          lease (BeamLisp.Env/retain_code! (BeamLisp.Vector/to_list (Map/get generation :modules)))]
      (BeamLisp.Ns.Rt/invoke (BeamLisp.Env/with_env :global
        (fn [] (BeamLisp.Env/fetch_exact! "proc.owner-registry" "register-supervisor!")))
        (list (erlang/self) lease))
      (BeamLisp.Env/install_supervisor_execution! lease)
      (BeamLisp.Env/complete_supervisor_start!))
    (Supervisor/init (erlang/element 4 argument) (erlang/element 5 argument))))
(defn- start_managed_tree [children options context]
  (let [admission (BeamLisp.Env/begin_supervisor_start!)]
    (try
      (BeamLisp.Env/launch_server_start! admission)
      (let [result (Supervisor/start_link :Elixir.BeamLisp.Supervisor
                     (tuple :bl_managed_supervisor admission context children options)
                     (Keyword/take options (list :name)))]
        (BeamLisp.Env/finish_server_start! admission result) result)
      (catch error
        (BeamLisp.Env/finish_server_start! admission :unknown)
        (erlang/raise __EXCEPTION_KIND__ error __STACKTRACE__)))))

(defn start_link
  "Start an ordinary or deferred supervision tree. Exactly one of :children
   and :children-factory is required. A reviewed zero-arity native function or
   fixed-zero Lisp Fn supplies the latter; evaluate it once at owner startup,
   after retaining its exact graph. Validate every child before starting any.
   Child restart specs keep the same captured context and retained generation."
  [spec]
  (let [own (erlang/element 2 (erlang/fun_info (fn [] nil) :module))
        fce (fn [fname arity]
              (erlang/error
                (Elixir.FunctionClauseError/exception
                  (list (tuple :module own) (tuple :function fname) (tuple :arity arity)))))
        vector? (fn [x]
                  (and (erlang/is_map x) (erlang/is_map_key :__struct__ x)
                       (erlang/== :"Elixir.BeamLisp.Vector" (erlang/map_get :__struct__ x))))
        normalize (fn [strategy]
                    (String/to_atom (String/replace (Atom/to_string strategy) "-" "_")))
        child-list (fn [children]
                     (if (vector? children) (BeamLisp.Vector/to_list children)
                       (if (erlang/is_list children) children (fce :child_list 1))))
        factory? (fn [value]
                   (or (erlang/is_function value 0)
                     (and (erlang/is_tuple value) (erlang/== 3 (erlang/tuple_size value))
                          (erlang/== :"$blfn" (erlang/element 1 value))
                          (erlang/is_map (erlang/element 2 value))
                          (erlang/== 1 (erlang/map_size (erlang/element 2 value)))
                          (erlang/is_map_key 0 (erlang/element 2 value))
                          (erlang/is_function (erlang/map_get 0 (erlang/element 2 value)) 0)
                          (erlang/== nil (erlang/element 3 value)))))
        intensity (fn [spec]
                    (let [given (Map/get spec :intensity)
                          items (if (vector? given) (erlang/map_get :items given) :no-items)]
                      (if (and (erlang/is_tuple items) (erlang/== 2 (erlang/tuple_size items)))
                        (list (tuple :max_restarts (erlang/element 1 items))
                              (tuple :max_seconds (erlang/element 2 items)))
                        (list))))
        match-error (fn [term]
                      (maps/put :term term
                        (maps/put :__exception__ true
                          (maps/put :__struct__ :"Elixir.MatchError" (maps/new)))))]
    (when (and (erlang/is_map spec) (erlang/is_map_key :children spec)
               (erlang/is_map_key :children-factory spec))
      (erlang/error :ambiguous_supervisor_children))
    (if (and (erlang/is_map spec) (erlang/is_map_key :strategy spec)
             (or (erlang/is_map_key :children spec) (erlang/is_map_key :children-factory spec)))
      (let [deferred? (erlang/is_map_key :children-factory spec)
            factory (Map/get spec :children-factory)
            _ (when (and deferred? (not (factory? factory)))
                (erlang/error :invalid_supervisor_children_factory))
            sup-opts (erlang/++ (list (tuple :strategy (normalize (erlang/map_get :strategy spec))))
                       (intensity spec))
            generation (Process/get :bl_generation)
            _ (when (and generation (not (BeamLisp.Env/executing_generation? generation)))
                (erlang/error :unadmitted_supervisor_starter))
            context (BeamLisp.Env/capture)
            _ (when deferred? (BeamLisp.Env/assert_managed_callback! generation factory))
            _ (when generation (BeamLisp.Env/ensure_sdk_owner_registry!))
            modules (Enum/uniq (erlang/++ (if generation (child-list (Map/get generation :modules)) (list))
                                         (if deferred? (BeamLisp.Env/callback_modules factory) (list))))
            lease (when (not (erlang/== (list) modules)) (BeamLisp.Env/retain_code! modules))]
        (try
          (let [children (child-list (if deferred?
                                      (try (BeamLisp.Ns.Rt/invoke factory (list))
                                        (finally (BeamLisp.Env/bind context)))
                                      (erlang/map_get :children spec)))
                ;; Construct all specs before Supervisor can start any child.
                ;; A descriptor cannot smuggle a managed raw MFA or borrow the
                ;; ambient environment of an earlier tree declaration.
                children (if generation
                           (erlang/element 1 (managed_children children context generation 0 4096))
                           children)
                result (if generation (start_managed_tree children sup-opts context)
                         (Supervisor/start_link children sup-opts))]
            (if (and (erlang/is_tuple result) (erlang/== 2 (erlang/tuple_size result))
                     (erlang/== :ok (erlang/element 1 result)))
              (let [pid (erlang/element 2 result)]
                (when (and lease (erlang/== nil generation))
                  (let [owned (BeamLisp.Env/transfer_code! lease pid)]
                    (when (erlang/== :cancelled owned) (erlang/error :supervisor_owner_died))))
                pid)
              (erlang/error (match-error result))))
          (finally
            (BeamLisp.Env/bind context)
            (when lease (BeamLisp.Env/release_code! lease)))))
      (fce :start_link 1))))
